          "description": "Executes a FHIR `create` interaction to persist a new resource of the specified type. It is required to supply the full resource payload in JSON form. Use this tool when you need to add new data (e.g., a new Patient or Observation). Note that servers may reject resources that violate profiles or mandatory bindings.",
