          "description": "Executes a standard FHIR `search` interaction on a given resource type, returning a bundle or list of matching resources. Use this when you need to query for multiple resources based on one or more search-parameters. Do not use this tool for create, update, or delete operations, and be aware that large result sets may be paginated by the FHIR server.",
